@@ -0,0 +1,12 @@
+# Research consulted
+
+Accessed 2026-08-14.
+
+- [VMware Product Interoperability Matrix](https://interopmatrix.broadcom.com/Interoperability) — checked the live product-combination authority used to confirm that target component pairs must be evaluated together, rather than treating each product upgrade independently.
+- [VMware Product Upgrade Path](https://interopmatrix.broadcom.com/Upgrade) — checked the live upgrade-path authority for source-to-target support before normalizing the frozen transitions used by this package.
+- [Update Sequence for VCF 9.0 and Compatible VMware Products](https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/390634/update-sequence-for-vcf-90-and-compatibl.html) — established the documented core ordering of SDDC Manager, NSX, vCenter, ESXi, and the later vSAN step, plus the special handling of Operations for Logs.
+- [Applying individual product updates to a VCF environment](https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/344935/applying-individual-product-updates-to-v.html) — checked the live tables that tie specific 8.x/4.x component updates to minimum future VCF targets and warn when an update has no 9.0 path.
+- [Upgrading to VCF 9.0 requires Distributed Switch](https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/430625/upgrading-to-vcf-90-requires-distributed.html) — established the VCF 9.0 vSphere Distributed Switch prerequisite used by the design.
+- [Converging VMware vSphere to VMware Cloud Foundation 9.0: The Top 10 Questions Answered](https://blogs.vmware.com/cloud-foundation/2026/04/16/converging-vmware-vsphere-to-vmware-cloud-foundation-9-0-the-top-10-questions-answered/) — established that VCF 9 does not support vSphere Lifecycle Manager baselines and requires the cluster to transition to image management.
+- [SddcSpec — VCF Installer API](https://developer.broadcom.com/xapis/vcf-installer-api/latest/data-structures/SddcSpec/) — cross-checked the live field descriptions, including `VCF_EXTEND` for connecting a secondary VCF instance to an existing fleet; the implementation remains pinned to the repository's vendored 9.0.0.0 schema.
+- [Deployment Pathways for VMware Cloud Foundation 9](https://blogs.vmware.com/cloud-foundation/2025/07/03/vcf-9-0-deployment-pathways/) — established the separation between adding capacity to an existing fleet and importing an existing vCenter deployment as a workload domain through VCF Operations.
